  reason: "The one producer arm for std.compiler_entry NativeClaimDriver programs (gunbc.target_binding NativeClaimProgramProducer { entry, deadline }). Its host part is only what no .dag fold can do: emit and build through the existing prepare_emitted_compiler_for_entry, spawn the built binary, wait up to the binding's std.measure Millisecond deadline, kill the child on expiry without admitting partial stdout, and otherwise carry stdout and status out unjudged. Every decision about what a completed report established -- the roster-to-row identity join, the status/rows agreement, held versus not held versus no observation -- is gunbc.native_claim_program native_claim_program_standing, evaluated by the host and mapped through cli_run classify_exit, so the host adds no verdict on the cases. Deadline expiry is mapped by the host to ObservationDidNotHold because the bound is part of the invocation's claim; the host does not invent the budget (it evaluates gunbc.instrument_targets native_claim_child_deadline_count at spawn, the Int projection via millisecond_count, and refuses NativeClaimDeadlineUngrounded when that read is absent or non-positive; gunbc.instrument_targets is listed in NATIVE_CLAIM_RUNTIME_AUTHORITY_MODULES the way the floor lists REQUIRED_FLOOR_RUNTIME_AUTHORITY_MODULES). It is ONE arm generic over entry: the next NativeClaimDriver program is a binding row, not another arm. The host file it sits in is the hand mirror gunbc.target_invocation_seed_growth already declares.",

